SDUSD::redeem
├── when requested shares exceeds maxRedeem for owner
│   └── it should revert with ERC4626ExceededMaxRedeem
└── when requested shares does not exceed maxRedeem for owner
    ├── when caller is neither owner nor sufficiently approved
    │   └── it should revert with ERC20InsufficientAllowance
    ├── when receiver is zero address
    │   └── it should revert with ERC20InvalidReceiver
    └── when caller is authorized
        ├── it should calculate assets to return by rounding down
        ├── it should decrease accountedAssets by the returned assets
        ├── it should decrease depositCapUsage by depositCapUsage times shares burned divided by pre-burn non-seed supply, rounded down
        ├── it should burn the requested shares from owner
        ├── it should transfer the calculated DUSD assets to receiver
        ├── it should return the calculated asset amount
        ├── it should emit Withdraw
        ├── it should not decrease the exchange rate because returned assets round down in favor of the vault
        ├── when caller is owner
        │   └── it should not require or spend an allowance
        ├── when caller is approved with a finite allowance
        │   └── it should decrease allowance by the redeemed shares
        ├── when caller is approved with maximum allowance
        │   └── it should leave the allowance unchanged
        ├── when requested shares is zero
        │   ├── it should complete without changing accounting, token balances, or share balances
        │   ├── it should leave depositCapUsage unchanged
        │   ├── it should leave the exchange rate unchanged
        │   └── it should emit Withdraw with zero assets and shares
        ├── when PAUSE_TYPE is paused
        │   └── it should remain available
        ├── when a reward period is active
        │   ├── it should return only the owner's share of currently unlocked assets
        │   ├── it should not make locked rewards withdrawable
        │   ├── it should retain enough DUSD in the vault to back all locked rewards
        │   ├── it should leave the reward amount and period boundaries unchanged
        │   ├── it should remove only the pooled principal represented by redeemed shares rather than all returned assets
        │   └── it should not decrease the remaining holders' exchange rate
        ├── when owner redeems their full balance
        │   ├── it should leave the permanent seed shares in total supply
        │   └── it should clear all pooled principal represented by non-seed shares
        ├── when shares are transferred before redemption
        │   ├── the transfer should leave depositCapUsage unchanged
        │   └── the recipient redemption should remove the transferred shares' proportional pooled principal
        ├── when deposits occur at different share prices
        │   └── it should pool principal across all non-seed shares, so an exiting depositor may remove less principal than they supplied
        └── when the vault has received a raw DUSD donation
            ├── it should not include the donation in returned assets
            ├── it should leave the exchange rate unchanged
            └── a subsequent redemption should not decrease the remaining holders' exchange rate
